# Lint and format what you staged, then the source-reading gates.
#
# `vp staged` is the right thing for a commit hook: it touches only the files in the commit and
# stays fast. The gates below are here for a reason that is easy to get wrong, so it is written
# down rather than assumed.
#
# **This repository has no git remote.** `pre-push` cannot fire, because there is nothing to
# push to, and GitHub Actions has never run for the same reason. Every protection the ship plan
# credits to CI — `vp check`, the tests, the build, the gates — is inert. The only automation
# that has ever actually executed on this repository is the line above.
#
# That is not theoretical either: the playground's build was broken by a `process.env.NODE_ENV`
# reference in source-linked framework code and stayed broken, unnoticed, while every in-package
# gate reported green.
#
# So the gates run here. All five read source, need no build, and take milliseconds together —
# cheap enough to pay per commit, which is the only event this repository actually has. They
# stay in `pre-push` and in CI as well, for when a remote exists.
#
# The dispatcher runs this under `sh -e`, so the first failing command aborts the commit.
# `VITE_GIT_HOOKS=0 git commit` skips it, if you must.

vp staged

node packages/infinite-canvas/scripts/verify-api-doc.mjs
node packages/infinite-canvas/scripts/verify-pure-core.mjs
node packages/infinite-canvas/scripts/verify-api-stability.mjs
node packages/infinite-canvas/scripts/verify-consumer-portability.mjs
